you've probably heard about spider-man  demon souls and assassin's creed  but what if i told you the one must play  title for ps5's launch lineup  is actually a game all ps5 owners get  for free  that's right astros playroom is a  wonderful adventure packed with  playstation nostalgia  and it's an absolute must play for  sony's new system  people of the internet's retroarching  tour here if we're meeting for the first  time  i'm just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and also stream over on twitch  we've been covering games here like  animal crossing and hogwarts legacy but  today is  all about astros playroom for the ps5  the playstation 5  is finally here at least if you can find  one that is  and while games like demon souls and  spider-man miles morales are sure to be  system sellers  you absolutely should not overlook  astros playroom  in short this game completely blew me  away it's also been great for my  six-year-old son who's a huge fan of  mario games  this is really his first introduction to  the world of playstation and to be  honest i  can't think of a better way for a kid to  learn all about playstation for the very  first time  in fact i love this game so much i think  it's the first one you should play  on your new system and that's exactly  what i told my wife's cousin when i  mailed his ps5 to him this week  that's right i actually got two ps5  pre-orders in somehow  you can check my twitter for details if  you want that story but i  tell you that so you know i'm not just  saying that for this video  that is real advice i gave someone play  astros playroom before  anything else on your ps5 in fact you  know what let me know your pre-order  story down in the comments below have  you tried  to pre-order a ps5 or xbox yet have you  been  successful in getting either of them  because  sadly it looks like a lot of people are  being left out to dry right now but let  me know  if you've had any luck you guys may  remember the playroom back  in 2013 on the ps4 astro was in that as  well  it's made by the same team and while it  was a fun little experience to show off  the ps4 camera frankly it was  really just that you actually couldn't  even play it at all without the camera  accessory  so i'm sure there's a large number of  people who never played it at all  because of that i can see how easy it  would be for new ps5 owners to maybe  overlook astros playroom  you should know though this time the  camera is not required to play the game  and you have  everything you need right inside the ps5  package  it just requires the new dual sense  controller and then the game itself will  be automatically installed on your  system  so what exactly is astros playroom if  this has been flying under your radar  well it's a  3d platforming adventure that will take  you through the history of playstation  you can probably beat it in about three  hours if you're really pushing and then  maybe four  to six somewhere in there if you're  trying to explore and see everything  it also serves as an incredible showcase  for the new dual sense controller  and i have to be honest with you guys i  never expected to be this blown away  by a controller the last time i remember  having this feeling with the controller  was back with the nintendo wii  and coincidentally it's pack in game wii  sports  now astro isn't likely to make  grandmothers run out to buy a ps5 or  have that same incredible mass market  appeal that the wii did  but for anyone who considers themselves  to be a fan of video games and you enjoy  playing on traditional controllers then  you absolutely have to  experience the duel sense it is truly  mind-blowing  it's really quite a shame that we can't  all just go out right now and try this  out in stores thanks to the ongoing  pandemic situation  but here's what really surprised me is  that i knew  going in okay astro is gonna be a  showcase for the playstation controller  the new dual sense i get that  but i didn't really expect it to be such  a phenomenal game around it  you'll move about a series of different  worlds that represent  generations of playstation consoles  astro will take on various enemies and  platform challenges along the way  you'll have a simple punch attack spin  attack and a laser when astro hovers to  help you take care of the enemies  there are plenty of collectibles to find  in each world as well  the two collectibles are puzzle pieces  and artifacts  the puzzle pieces you find are added to  a giant puzzle in the game's hub area  whereas the artifacts are pieces of  playstation's history that also make  their way  into the hub and if you're wondering why  i'm not showing any footage of the  puzzle pieces and of the artifacts i  think it's  gonna be much better honestly if you  discover this stuff on your own it's  it's  super fun to see all the little details  in there one of my favorite things is  when my son was playing and he'd unlock  a new artifact and kind of give that  look of of what in the world is this  and then i would get to launch into a  story explaining like oh yeah i remember  when i bought this and when we were  hanging out at fred's birthday we played  that it's just there are so many moments  like that especially if you're  kind of around the age i am right now  maybe you remember the original  playstation you've got kids of your own  now  that is uh it's just so many great  stories that came out of that  i would argue that it's all of those  tiny little details of the nostalgia  that  really helped put this game over the top  there's so many little nods and secrets  that i just  frankly don't want to spoil them here  it'll be far better for you to  experience it yourself  it will only take you about four to six  hours to complete all the levels and  gather  all the collectibles as i said in the  beginning honestly that's  probably the only problem i had with the  game i wish it was longer  after it was over i wanted even more  both my son and i were kind of sad to  see it come to an end but what an  incredible ride it was along the way  hopefully this is only the beginning for  astro on ps5 i would honestly  love to see a sobe team get a shot at  making a full length  3d platformer even one featuring astro  as always guys thank you so much for  watching  i'll talk to you again soon
 

